# Anaphoric pronouns and demonstratives: they stand in for a person or thing
# named earlier in the conversation, never for an article title. Checked by
# WikipediaSkill._is_anaphoric (an exact-value match, never substring
# containment) before a {query} value is looked up, so a real title that
# merely contains one of these words as a word ("the it crowd", "her
# majesty") is never rejected.
(ele|ela|isso|eles)
(ele|ela|eles)
(seu|sua|deles)
(isso|isto|esses|estes)
